{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.IsospinMirrorInvariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.IsospinMirrorInvariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.isospinExchange_det_mirror_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.isospinExchange_det_mirror_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/IsospinMirrorInvariance.lean#L56-L64","doc":"**Strong-sector mirror invariance.** The isospin-signed exchange\ndeterminant is invariant under the global proton↔neutron mirror.  Hence\nany strong binding functional of this determinant assigns a mirror pair\n(³H and ³He) the same value: the strong ³H/³He split is exactly zero, so\nthe observed ~1.10× split is non-strong (the Coulomb term). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.isospinExchange_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.isospinExchange_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/IsospinMirrorInvariance.lean#L45-L54","doc":"The global isospin mirror `s ↦ -s` (proton ↔ neutron on every\nnucleon) fixes every entry of the strong exchange matrix, since\n`(-s i)(-s j) = s i * s j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.isospinExchange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.isospinExchange","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/IsospinMirrorInvariance.lean#L37-L43","doc":"Strong isospin-signed exchange matrix: diagonal `1`, off-diagonal\nbond `mag i j * s i * s j`, where `s : Fin n → R` is the nucleon isospin\nlabelling (`+1` proton / `-1` neutron, kept generic) and `mag i j` is the\nisospin-independent, geometry-only bond magnitude. ","signatureChunk":0}]}